47.531, 47.566, 48.158, 48.216, 48.262, 48.286, 48.344, 48.39, 48.46, 48.518, 48.576, 48.622, 48.657, 48.727, 48.785, 48.831, 48.889, 48.947, 49.005, 49.098, 49.168, 49.226, 49.272, 49.342, 49.423, 49.574, 50.004, 50.05, 50.097, 50.132, 50.201, 50.259, 50.329, 50.445, 50.515, 50.608, 50.758, 50.875, 50.979, 51.025, 51.049, 51.118, 51.188, 51.281, 51.362, 51.478, 51.641, 52.245]}, "text": "Ice Age Sicily had elephants, and island life shrank them until the smallest stood under a metre. You could have looked one in the eye.\n\nTheir bones have turned up in caves on Sicily and Malta. Head-on, the skull shows two small eye sockets at the sides, and in the middle, one enormous hole.\n\nIn 1914, a palaeontologist named Abel imagined sailors finding a skull like this in a beach cave. He thought it might be where the Cyclops came from.\n\nHere is our version. A sailor ducks in to light a fire.\n\n\"Hello?\" the sailor asked.\n\nIn the clay, something looks back at him. One enormous eye.\n\n\"Nope.\"\n\nThe sailor is imagined. The skulls are real."}